, the record here runs 75 years, from 1951 to 2025, on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 7 grids. September to October, October to November and November to December each came in under 90% of normal in 37 of those years. In 2025, October to November was 59% of normal on the middle of the grids, and in 2026 so far March to April was 31% of normal while May to June hit 235%. Every grid had its driest year in 1954, with grid 13077 down at 50% of normal.</p>"}
